# Baseline security headers for every page (Netlify serves this from the publish dir).
# Added 2026-08-21 from the security scan (M2); tightened 2026-10-08 (sec/site-hardening).
#  - X-Frame-Options SAMEORIGIN + CSP frame-ancestors 'self': blocks clickjacking by
#    other sites. NOT DENY: /investor-pitch/demo frames our own /brain-viz/index.html,
#    and DENY blocked that same-origin iframe. (This governs OTHERS framing us; it does
#    NOT stop us embedding Turnstile / Calendly / GTM iframes, which is us->them.)
#  - HSTS has NO includeSubDomains / preload on purpose: oscen.ai has live
#    subdomains (crm/demo/dashboard/links) and preload is hard to undo. Apex/www only.
#  - Enforced CSP is limited to directives that cannot break third-party scripts
#    (frame-ancestors, object-src, base-uri). The full source allowlist ships as
#    Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: watch the browser console on every page
#    (pixels firing, Turnstile, Calendly, brain-viz, fonts) before promoting it.
#    GTM can inject arbitrary tags, so any new GTM tag may need a host added here.
#    The fh-*.ecs.us-west-2.on.aws host is the Meta Conversions API Gateway the Meta
#    pixel config posts every event to (found 2026-10-09); a new gateway means a new host.
#  - Permissions-Policy denies powerful features the site never uses. Clipboard and
#    Web Share stay allowed (the /support referral button uses them).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=(), bluetooth=(), midi=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=(), browsing-topics=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://connect.facebook.net https://analytics.tiktok.com https://static.ads-twitter.com https://www.redditstatic.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://assets.calendly.com https://plausible.io https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://assets.calendly.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://crm.oscen.ai https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.facebook.com https://connect.facebook.net https://*.tiktok.com https://*.tiktokw.us https://*.reddit.com https://www.redditstatic.com https://*.twitter.com https://*.x.com https://static.ads-twitter.com https://plausible.io https://buttondown.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://calendly.com https://*.calendly.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://fh-118116076e9a4c2a96a99fbb70bea2a0.ecs.us-west-2.on.aws; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://calendly.com https://*.calendly.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.facebook.com https://demo.oscen.ai; worker-src 'self' blob:; form-action 'self' https://buttondown.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

# Internal / unlisted pages: keep them out of search even if a URL leaks.
# (robots.txt Disallow alone does not deindex a linked URL; this header does.)
/dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/investor-pitch/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
